If you have an ethical problem with deleting that file; just start a
couple games, proceed into the mines, get killed, rinse repeat, until
that bones file is removed. This is certainly possible because the
bones are yet on a shallow level. Given that this procedure solves
your problem naturally anyway, I'd just erase the one file as described
above, to not waste time, in case you think to have no chance to survive
it.

You gave the impression that there's no way WRT your skill to solve the
problem. You may want to consider, though, to skip that level, e.g. by
digging through the floor, and on your way up circumvent those threats.
Or ignore the mines, if you see that the bones file is loaded - you know
that bones files are not always loaded? - and solve the game without the
mines' features. Once you see that you miss some essentials in your game,
say, no general shop, or no altar, you can always come back and do the
mines, then.

